$2 21. Qxd5 cxd5 22. Rxc7 Bd6 {Source: Bernard Cafferty. "My game against L.
Rosselson, William Ellis School, Highgate, came in the 10th and last round of
the above contest, on April 26th, 1952. It was hardly a sterling effort on his
part. LR finished on 6 pts, compared to the 7.5 of Peter Gibbs, myself and
Peter Sanderson. The tie was never broken, as players had made travel
arrangements to leave on the next day (or the same day for some?). I had
beaten PCG in the 4th round and drew with PDS in the 8th."} 1-0

